      "content": "217|### Dopendis Gravebreath\n218|\n219|Dopendis Gravebreath was a powerful mage and secret adherent of [[Orcus]], obsessed with the boundary between life and death. His research was part of the same cult operation later exposed at [[Blacklung Quarry]], but his role was separate: he developed soul jars and refined the trapped dead into **[[Soul Diesel]]**, a necromantic fuel the cult hoped to use in a mass raise dead ritual. The cult’s promised reward was not wealth or immortality, but an army of the dead.\n220|\n221|He believed souls weren't merely spiritual entities.\n222|\n223|They were **energy**.\n224|\n225|Energy that could be collected.\n226|\n227|Stored.\n228|\n229|And eventually consumed.\n230|\n231|He constructed this laboratory to develop vessels capable of trapping souls before they could reach the afterlife.\n232|\n233|His writings repeatedly refer to something called:\n234|\n235|**\"The Great Working.\"**\n236|\n237|Apparently, Dopendis Gravebreath intended to gather hundreds, perhaps thousands, of souls to power a ritual.\n238|\n239|Exactly what that ritual would accomplish isn't explained.\n240|\n241|Dopendis Gravebreath's current whereabouts are unknown.\n242|",
