      "hasMoreBelow": false,
      "nextStartLine": null,
      "content": "1|# Adventure Summary\n2|\n3|**Dread and Breakfast** is a monster-hunt adventure set in the [[Grim Forest]], a dangerous woodland within [[The Outback]] of [[Stickyickistan]]. Travelers and caravans have begun disappearing along the Neck, a trade route connecting [[North Booftown]] with inland settlements such as [[Doobius House]]. The characters are hired to investigate the disappearances and uncover the truth behind a welcoming roadside tavern that is far more alive than it appears.\n4|\n5|The adventure culminates in a three-wave encounter inside a tavern mimic. Characters should be prepared for a strange, dangerous fight involving smaller mimics, shrinking magic, acid, and a creature that cannot be harmed from outside.\n6|\n7|# The Rolling Papers Advertisement\n8|\n9|**Submitted by:** [[Nevercough Tribunal]]    \n10|**Tier:** Tier 1  \n11|**Recommended Level:** 3  \n12|**Expected Length:** One-shot, approximately 3–4 hours  \n13|**Tone:** Forest horror, monster investigation, biomantic weirdness, dark comedy  \n14|**Location:** [[Grim Forest]] / The Neck  \n15|\n16|## Headline\n17|\n18|> **TRAVELERS MISSING ALONG THE NECK: LICENSED HUNTERS REQUESTED**\n19|\n20|## Public Notice\n21|\n22|Caravans and travelers have disappeared along the trade route through the [[Grim Forest]]. The [[Nevercough Tribunal]] seeks capable adventurers to investigate the disappearances, protect future caravans, and remove the creature responsible.\n23|\n24|[[Dr. Stein]] offers additional compensation for the recovery of his missing laboratory or the safe return of his half-brother, [[Jonjo Starr]].\n25|\n26|Applicants should report to the northern road station at the edge of the Grim Forest. Ask for the biomancy researcher with the metal lungs.\n27|\n28|# What Players Should Know\n29|\n30|- **Content / vibe:** Forest horror, missing travelers, acid, body horror, biomantic experiments, mimics, and dark comedy.\n31|- **Combat / roleplay / exploration mix:** Investigation and tracking followed by a dangerous three-wave combat encounter.\n32|- **Character hooks:** Good for monster hunters, caravan guards, Free League contractors, researchers, bounty hunters, or adventurers seeking payment and unusual monster components.\n33|- **Special notes:** The party will investigate the Grim Forest and track the creature through dangerous terrain. Expect little downtime between combat waves.\n34|\n35|# Rewards\n36|\n37|- **250 gp per character** for restoring safety to the Neck.\n38|- **125 gp per character** for finding Dr. Stein’s brother.\n39|- **600 XP** each\n40|- Possible future work from [[Dr. Stein]], the [[Nevercough Tribunal]], or the [[Tribunal Highblade Coalition]].\n41|- The opportunity to harvest unusual mimic components for crafting.\n42|\n43|# Sign-Up\n44|\n45|**DM:** Initiate of Tribulation, Vorg Lordcaster \n46|**Date / Time:** TBD  \n47|**Seats:** 4–5 players  \n48|**How to join:** Register through the [[FLS Guildhall]] or post in the Free League chat.\n49|",
