      "content": "1|[[Unit BH-Umbra Δ9]] has been arrested. An up and coming ragtag heist crew of the [[Ashen Shadow Society]] has been assigned to break them out.\n2|\n3|I want to convert the adventure \"Prisoner 13\" from the book Keys From the Golden Vault where the Ashen Shadow Society is acting as the patron. Instead of trying to get a key from a prisoner, they actually have to break out 4 prisoners. The players will be playing both as the heist crew, and as the prisoners that need to be broken out. The heist crew is 4 level 4s, and the prisoners are 4 level 8s.\n4|\n5|# The 4 Prisoners of A.S.S.C.U.N.T\n6|\n7|_An Adventure for four 4th-level infiltrators and four 8th-level prisoners_\n8|\n9|[[Unit BH-Umbra Δ9]], the first recognized Bloodhound squad of the [[Ashen Shadow Society Creature Utilisation & Neutralisation Taskforce]], has been arrested and imprisoned in one of [[Mythmos]]’s most secure detention sites. The [[Ashen Shadow Society]] wants the squad back before its members, contacts, field notes, and recovered specimens become someone else’s property. Rather than risk a Raven or Shadowsong squad on a politically radioactive extraction, the Society assigns the job to an expendable support crew hungry enough to prove they belong, or maybe just stupid enough to play along.\n10|\n11|In this adventure, the players control both sides of the operation: four 4th-level support-squad infiltrators working their way into the prison from outside, and four 8th-level members of [[Unit BH-Umbra Δ9]] fighting, scheming, and surviving from within. The infiltrators must create openings, smuggle tools, sabotage defenses, and locate the prisoners. The prisoners must exploit those openings, mislead guards, survive lockdowns, and break themselves out when the moment comes.\n12|\n13|![[Pasted image 20260824210834.png]]\n14|\n15|_Perched on a windswept bluff is the prison, [[Giantfrost Penitentiary]], wherein awaits [[Unit BH-Umbra Δ9]]_\n16|\n17|## Adventure Background\n18|\n19|[[Unit BH-Umbra Δ9]] is the first recognized Bloodhound squad of the [[Ashen Shadow Society Creature Utilisation & Neutralisation Taskforce]], the Society’s specialized monster-capture, specimen-harvesting, and creature-neutralization branch. Its members have survived missions involving criminal syndicates, unstable arcane artifacts, hostile cults, and dangerous creatures from [[The Outback]]. That success made them valuable to the [[Ashen Shadow Society]], but it also made them visible.\n20|\n21|During a job outside Stickyickistan, Unit BH-Umbra Δ9 was captured and transferred to **Giantfrost Penitentiary**, a remote detention fortress in the northernmost reaches of Mythmos. Built into a frozen mountain stronghold surrounded by killing cold, high cliffs, and miles of white wilderness, Giantfrost uses altitude, isolation, and weather as part of its security. It is where distant authorities send prisoners too dangerous, politically inconvenient, or magically troublesome to keep anywhere warmer.\n22|\n23|The Ashen Shadow Society wants the squad recovered before its members, field notes, contacts, and harvested specimens become someone else’s property. The Society is not acting out of loyalty. Unit BH-Umbra Δ9 knows too much about the Ashen Citadel, ASSCUNT field protocols, Society clients, illicit component markets, and contracts the Society would prefer not to explain in court.\n24|\n25|Rather than risk a Raven or Shadowsong squad on a politically radioactive extraction, the Society assigns the job to an up-and-coming support crew. Officially, the crew is being given a chance to prove it belongs among the real squads. Unofficially, it is expendable. If the heist succeeds, the Society gets its Bloodhounds back. If it fails, the Council of Shadows can deny the operation, disavow the crew, and let Giantfrost Penitentiary keep the bodies.\n26|\n27|## Adventure Hooks\n28|\n29|After years of financial hardship due to their stolen fortune, the mountain dwarves of Clan Axebreaker have located the lost treasure but have been unable to access it. A representative of the clan, Varrin Axebreaker, wishes to hire the characters to learn how to access the treasure. If you’re not using the Golden Vault as a patron (see “Using the Golden Vault” below), here are some possible ways Varrin learned about the characters:\n30|\n31|**By Reputation.** Varrin learned of the characters in the aftermath of a previous adventure, especially one that involved retrieving a person or treasure from a dangerous location.\n32|\n33|**Mutual Acquaintance.** One of the characters’ patrons is an old acquaintance of Varrin’s and arranged the meeting. If the characters are involved with the Golden Vault, use this option.\n34|\n35|**Trial Run.** Varrin was responsible for a previous adventure the characters completed successfully. It was a test to see if they were worthy of this mission.",
